;=====================================================================
; melamine_refined.itp
; Melamine (1,3,5-triazine-2,4,6-triamine) - OPLS-AA
;
; BASE: LigParGen 1.14*CM1A-LBCC (charges, LJ, dihedrals UNCHANGED)
;
; MODIFICATIONS (bonded terms only):
;   [A] Equilibrium geometry r0, theta0 from COD 2205105
;       Cousson, Nicolai & Fillaux, Acta Cryst. E 61 (2005) o222
;       14 K neutron diffraction
;   [B] Stretch force constants from Fernandez-Liencres, Navarro,
;       Lopez-Gonzalez, Fernandez-Gomez, Tomkinson & Kearley,
;       Chem. Phys. 266 (2001) 1-17, Table 4 (refined values)
;
; UNIT CONVERSION USED:
;   1 aJ/A^2 = 1e-18 J * 6.02214e23 /mol * 100 nm^-2
;            = 60221.4 kJ mol^-1 nm^-2
;   Both F (spectroscopic) and kb (GROMACS) use V = 1/2 k dr^2,
;   so the conversion is direct with no factor of 2.
;
; DERIVATIONS (see notes at bottom of file)
;   f(N-H)    = 6.545 aJ/A^2  -> 394150 kJ/mol/nm^2
;   f(C-Na)   = 7.816 aJ/A^2  -> 470690 kJ/mol/nm^2
;   f(ring)   = ~7.8  aJ/A^2  -> 469700 (NOT uniquely determined - see notes)
;
; STAGING: apply in this order, re-running EM + NVT between stages,
; and check the vDoS after each:
;   Stage 1 = [A] geometry only        (highest confidence)
;   Stage 2 = [A] + N-H kb             (rigorously derived)
;   Stage 3 = [A] + N-H + C-Na kb      (2x2 solve, well founded)
;   Stage 4 = + ring kb                (SPECULATIVE - may worsen ~1710)
;
; Stage 3 is the recommended default. Ring kb is commented out.
;=====================================================================

