;=====================================================================
; DERIVATION NOTES
;=====================================================================
;
; READING TABLE 4 (Fernandez-Liencres et al. 2001, p.11)
;   The table is LOWER TRIANGULAR, printed row by row.
;   The DIAGONAL element is the LAST number in each row.
;   Refined values are in parentheses; pre-refinement HF/3-21G values
;   are outside. Use the parenthesised (refined) values.
;   Example - row "F3,3  -0.056  0.100  6.294(6.537)" means
;     F3,1 = -0.056 ; F3,2 = 0.100 ; F3,3 = 6.294 (refined 6.537)
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------
; 1) N-H STRETCH  (rigorous)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------
; N-H stretching appears in four independent symmetry blocks
; (Table 3, p.6):
;     S3  = (R10+R11+R12+R13+R14+R15)/sqrt(6)      A1'
;     S7  = (R10-R11+R12-R13+R14-R15)/sqrt(6)      A2'
;     S12 = (2R10-R11-R12-R13-R14+2R15)/sqrt(12)   E'
;     S13 = (R11-R12-R13+R14)/2                    E'
;
; Refined diagonals:
;     F3,3   = 6.537
;     F7,7   = 6.518
;     F12,12 = 6.523
;     F13,13 = 6.603
;
; All four agree to within 1.3%. For a normalized symmetric
; combination, F_SS = f_diag + (sum of interaction constants).
; Agreement across all four blocks therefore PROVES the N-H/N-H
; interaction constants are ~0, so F_SS = f(N-H) directly.
;
;     f(N-H) = mean = 6.545 aJ/A^2
;     kb     = 6.545 * 60221.4 = 394150 kJ/mol/nm^2
;
; NORMALIZATION CHECK: Table 3 writes S1, S2, S3 as plain sums
; without explicit 1/sqrt(N) factors. If they were truly
; unnormalized, f(N-H) would be 6.537/6 = 1.09 aJ/A^2, which is
; physically impossible for an N-H bond (~6.5 expected).
; The normalized reading is therefore the correct one.
;
; HARMONIC FREQUENCY CHECK (reduced mass 0.9403 amu):
;     LigParGen  363171 kJ/mol/nm^2 -> 603.0 N/m -> 3299 cm^-1
;     Refined    394150 kJ/mol/nm^2 -> 654.5 N/m -> 3437 cm^-1
;     Experiment (Table 5): 3378, 3381, 3497, 3498 cm^-1
;     Your MD peaks:        3257, 3364, 3379 cm^-1
;   -> the correction moves the N-H region toward experiment.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------
; 2) EXOCYCLIC C-Na STRETCH  (2x2 solve)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------
;     S2  = (R7+R8+R9)/sqrt(3)          A1'   -> F2,2   = 6.670
;     S11 = (2R7-R8-R9)/sqrt(6)         E'    -> F11,11 = 8.389
;
; For three equivalent bonds with a single interaction constant f':
;     F2,2   = f + 2f'
;     F11,11 = f -  f'
;
; Solving:
;     f'          = (F2,2 - F11,11)/3 = -0.573 aJ/A^2
;     f(C-Na)     = F11,11 + f'       =  7.816 aJ/A^2
;     kb          = 7.816 * 60221.4   =  470690 kJ/mol/nm^2
;
; The large negative f' reflects through-ring conjugation between
; the three exocyclic bonds, consistent with the resonance picture.
;
; SANITY: f = 7.82 aJ/A^2 corresponds to ~50% double-bond character,
; appropriate for a 1.347 A conjugated C-N. LigParGen's 5.93 aJ/A^2
; corresponds closer to a pure C-N single bond, which is wrong for
; melamine.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------
; 3) RING C-N STRETCH  (NOT uniquely determined)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------
;     S1 = (R1+..+R6)/sqrt(6)                A1' -> F1,1  = 11.836
;     S6 = (R1-R2+R3-R4+R5-R6)/sqrt(6)       A2' -> F6,6  =  4.390
;     S10 (E', mixed combination)                -> F10,10=  7.663
;
; With ortho/meta/para interaction constants:
;     F1,1 = f + 2f_o + 2f_m + f_p
;     F6,6 = f - 2f_o + 2f_m - f_p
;
;     Sum:  f + 2f_m       = 8.113
;     Diff: 2f_o + f_p     = 3.723
;
; Two equations, four unknowns. Not solvable without the full E'
; block expansion and the B-matrix. Bracketed estimate 7.7-8.1.
; Left at the LigParGen value by default. See Stage 4 warning.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------
; 4) WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT TRANSFERRED
; ---------------------------------------------------------------
; (a) ALL off-diagonal force constants. GROMACS bonded terms are
;     diagonal and separable. The refined off-diagonals
;     (F18,11 = 0.923, F14,10 = 0.745, F16,11 = -0.224, ...) are
;     exactly what generates the mixed NH-rock / CN-stretch modes
;     at 1148-1180 cm^-1 (Table 5, nu8/nu15). This is the structural
;     reason your MD has a hole at 1100-1400 cm^-1, and it CANNOT be
;     repaired by editing diagonal terms.
;
; (b) All bend and torsion constants. Table 4's caption gives aJ/A^2
;     throughout, but bends require aJ/rad^2 and the reference-length
;     scaling convention is not stated. Converting them would be
;     guesswork.
;
; (c) The authors state (p.2-3) that only intramolecular constants
;     were defined, "neglecting the intermolecular forces among the
;     melamine and the neighbouring molecules," giving an EFFECTIVE
;     force field. They also refined under an assumed D3h symmetry
;     which the crystal does not possess.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------
; 5) SEPARATE RESULT USEFUL FOR LEAPR
; ---------------------------------------------------------------
; The same paper (Section 4.3, p.15-16) reports the Debye-Waller
; anisotropy needed to reproduce the INS intensities:
;
;     in-plane  DW = 0.010     (force constant 59.12 kcal/A^2)
;     out-of-plane DW = 0.040  (force constant 28.96 kcal/A^2)
;     ratio = 4
;
; This is directly usable when constructing S(alpha,beta), and is
; independent of whether you adopt any of the force constants above.
;
;=====================================================================
; REFERENCES
;=====================================================================
; Fernandez-Liencres, M.P.; Navarro, A.; Lopez-Gonzalez, J.J.;
;   Fernandez-Gomez, M.; Tomkinson, J.; Kearley, G.J.
;   "Measurement and ab initio modeling of the inelastic neutron
;   scattering of solid melamine. Evidence of the anisotropy in the
;   external modes spectrum."
;   Chemical Physics 266 (2001) 1-17.
;   doi:10.1016/S0301-0104(01)00326-3
;
; Cousson, A.; Nicolai, B.; Fillaux, F.
;   Acta Crystallographica Section E 61 (2005) o222-o224.
;   doi:10.1107/S160053680403332X   [COD entry 2205105]
;
; Hughes, E.W. J. Am. Chem. Soc. 63 (1941) 1737-1752.
;   doi:10.1021/ja01851a021
;
; Dodda, L.S.; Cabeza de Vaca, I.; Tirado-Rives, J.; Jorgensen, W.L.
;   Nucleic Acids Research 45 (2017) W331-W336.  [LigParGen]
;=====================================================================
